,"user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-23T18:02:34Z","updated_at":"2025-05-23T18:02:34Z","body":"Will be fixed by https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102552\n","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2905375058/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":1,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2905421305","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/106757#issuecomment-2905421305","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106757","id":2905421305,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6tLTX5","user":{"login":"jamie-pate","id":682658,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY4MjY1OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/682658?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jamie-pate","html_url":"https://github.com/jamie-pate","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jamie-pate/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jamie-pate/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jamie-pate/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jamie-pate/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jamie-pate/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jamie-pate/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jamie-pate/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jamie-pate/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jamie-pate/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-23T18:30:15Z","updated_at":"2025-05-23T19:45:08Z","body":"MTLCompilerService will run for ~4 minutes when loading a level in my project, which is an order of magnitude worse than vulkan (~though metal frame rate is way faster in the end, so vulkan on M1 is not a good workaround~ After doing some benchmarks vulkan gives roughly the same frame rates)\n\n`<mygame> --world=2 --benchmark` (first run)\n`--rendering-driver metal`:  54.17s user 25.63s system 12% cpu 10:31.56 total\n`--rendering-driver vulkan`: 13.08s user 3.28s system 9% cpu 2:54.45 total\n\n\nAlso, precompiling the export shader cache won't help developers on M1 using the editor. It will still need to run MTLCompilerService when you open the project","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2905421305/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2905561292","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/106757#issuecomment-2905561292","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106757","id":2905561292,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6tL1jM","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-23T19:19:17Z","updated_at":"2025-05-23T19:19:41Z","body":"> Also, precompiling the export shader cache won't help developers on M1 using the editor. It will still need to run MTLCompilerService when you open the project\n\nI wonder if the shader baker could be used to ship a precompiled shader cache with official editor binaries. This will increase download size somewhat (a few MB when compressed), but it'd certainly improve the first-time user experience.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2905561292/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2905607370","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/106757#issuecomment-2905607370","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106757","id":2905607370,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6tMAzK","user":{"login":"jamie-pate","id":682658,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY4MjY1OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/682658?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jamie-pate","html_url":"https://github.com/jamie-pate","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jamie-pate/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jamie-pate/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jamie-pate/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jamie-pate/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jamie-pate/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jamie-pate/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jamie-pate/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jamie-pate/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jamie-pate/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-23T19:39:53Z","updated_at":"2025-05-23T19:39:53Z","body":"> a precompiled shader cache with official editor binaries\n\nthis wouldn't help because they'd still have to compile shaders when they open their project (the first time)\n\nI guess it's not a huge deal because developers will only pay the cost on the first load of their project, and open the project many many times afterward...\n\nFor the exported  game it's much more important to have the shaders precompiled so the end users have a good experience","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2905607370/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2905788707","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/106757#issuecomment-2905788707","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106757","id":2905788707,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6tMtEj","user":{"login":"stuartcarnie","id":52852,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyODUy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52852?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie","html_url":"https://github.com/stuartcarnie","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-23T20:54:07Z","updated_at":"2025-05-23T20:54:30Z","body":"@jamie-pate you can also try setting the following environment variable, as Vulkan defers compiling / loading until the pipeline is created, so that actually is more likely to cause stutters during gameplay.\n\nThe following will cause the Metal driver to operate similarly, only compiling the pipelines that are created by Godot (and is the default behaviour for Apple embedded platforms, like iOS):\n\n```\nGODOT_MTL_SHADER_LOAD_STRATEGY=lazy\n```\n\nLet us know how that goes.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2905788707/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2905859731","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/106757#issuecomment-2905859731","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106757","id":2905859731,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6tM-aT","user":{"login":"jamie-pate","id":682658,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY4MjY1OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/682658?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jamie-pate","html_url":"https://github.com/jamie-pate","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jamie-pate/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jamie-pate/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jamie-pate/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jamie-pate/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jamie-pate/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jamie-pate/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jamie-pate/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jamie-pate/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jamie-pate/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-23T21:29:30Z","updated_at":"2025-05-23T21:31:14Z","body":"@stuartcarnie wouldn't the [Ubershaders](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/tutorials/performance/pipeline_compilations.html#reducing-stutter-from-shader-pipeline-compilations) feature make `GODOT_MTL_SHADER_LOAD_STRATEGY=lazy` the desired behavior?\n\nAlso shouldn't this be exposed as a project setting instead? :D\n\nResults agree with your hypothesis:\n`sudo rm -r /var/folders/*/*/*/com.mycorp.*/com.apple.metal*`\n`export GODOT_MTL_SHADER_LOAD_STRATEGY=lazy`\n`<mygame> --rendering-driver metal -- --world=2 --benchmark` 17.75s user 6.19s system 17% cpu 2:15.87 total\n\nGot some weird artifacts though\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/cec30508-18c2-471b-a28e-3da4789f55b7)","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2905859731/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2905932916","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/106757#issuecomment-2905932916","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106757","id":2905932916,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6tNQR0","user":{"login":"jamie-pate","id":682658,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY4MjY1OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/682658?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jamie-pate","html_url":"https://github.com/jamie-pate","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jamie-pate/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jamie-pate/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jamie-pate/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jamie-pate/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jamie-pate/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jamie-pate/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jamie-pate/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jamie-pate/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jamie-pate/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-23T22:20:13Z","updated_at":"2025-05-23T22:21:00Z","body":"Compilations from the godot monitor over the course of the benchmark (camera travels through the level across 12 waypoints)\n'Count' is the current waypoint counter\n'Level' is the current quality level setting\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/eb951117-9259-4f83-a9df-c0d44cb06071)\n\nWhen auto-quality is enabled (enables-disables features) it causes extra compilations by altering the material settings","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2905932916/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2907005451","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/106757#issuecomment-2907005451","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106757","id":2907005451,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6tRWIL","user":{"login":"stuartcarnie","id":52852,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyODUy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52852?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie","html_url":"https://github.com/stuartcarnie","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-24T20:16:56Z","updated_at":"2025-05-24T20:16:56Z","body":"> Also shouldn't this be exposed as a project setting instead? :D\n\nNo, as it was a development feature to compare the differing strategies. We ended up making it the default (and only) behaviour for embedded (iOS, visionOS) platforms.\n\n> Got some weird artifacts though\n\nThat is surprising. I wouldn't expect that to be caused by the `lazy` option, as it is only delaying compilation to when the pipeline is first created by the engine; it doesn't alter the shader source or pipeline in any way.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2907005451/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2924099796","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/106757#issuecomment-2924099796","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106757","id":2924099796,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6uSjjU","user":{"login":"jamie-pate","id":682658,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY4MjY1OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/682658?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jamie-pate","html_url":"https://github.com/jamie-pate","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jamie-pate/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jamie-pate/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jamie-pate/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jamie-pate/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jamie-pate/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jamie-pate/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jamie-pate/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jamie-pate/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jamie-pate/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-31T03:10:54Z","updated_at":"2025-05-31T03:10:54Z","body":"For anyone reading this, the best combo I found was `vulkan` + `mobile`\n\n```\ntime ./Ultimate\\ Fabric\\ Challenge\\ 3.app/Contents/MacOS/Ultimate\\ Fabric\\ Challenge  --no-capture-mouse -- --benchmark --world=2 --benchmark-count=2 \n 10.98s user 2.71s system 26% cpu 51.898 total \n```","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2924099796/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3477156134","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/106757#issuecomment-3477156134","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106757","id":3477156134,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7PQTEm","user":{"login":"1000nettles","id":425298,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQyNTI5OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/425298?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/1000nettles","html_url":"https://github.com/1000nettles","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/1000nettles/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/1000nettles/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/1000nettles/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/1000nettles/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/1000nettles/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/1000nettles/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/1000nettles/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/1000nettles/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/1000nettles/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-02T02:18:59Z","updated_at":"2025-11-02T02:18:59Z","body":"I am also seeing large load times when using Metal on projects and loading them in the editor.\n\n### Tested versions\n\nReproducible on v4.5.1-stable with Metal rendering\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.5.1.stable - macOS Tahoe (26.0.1) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - Metal 3.2 - Forward+ - Apple M4 Pro (Apple9)\n\n----\n\nThe Material Tester project is a good one because it's extra apparent in there, to the tune of needing to wait almost 2 minutes for the scene to load in the editor (no previously cached shaders.) Vulkan is way faster here, which takes less than 10 seconds.\n\nWhen I export the Material Tester project with shader baking, it actually loads very quickly, about 10 seconds (I made sure shader caches were deleted before testing.)\n\n\n\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3477156134/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3694668096","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/106757#issuecomment-3694668096","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106757","id":3694668096,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7cOClA","user":{"login":"Mike-Litton","id":152016512,"node_id":"U_kgDOCQ-WgA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/152016512?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mike-Litton","html_url":"https://github.com/Mike-Litton","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mike-Litton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mike-Litton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mike-Litton/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mike-Litton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mike-Litton/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mike-Litton/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mike-Litton/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mike-Litton/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mike-Litton/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-28T11:20:36Z","updated_at":"2025-12-28T11:20:36Z","body":"> [@stuartcarnie](https://github.com/stuartcarnie) wouldn't the [Ubershaders](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/tutorials/performance/pipeline_compilations.html#reducing-stutter-from-shader-pipeline-compilations) feature make `GODOT_MTL_SHADER_LOAD_STRATEGY=lazy` the desired behavior?\n> \n> Also shouldn't this be exposed as a project setting instead? :D\n> \n> Results agree with your hypothesis: `sudo rm -r /var/folders/*/*/*/com.mycorp.*/com.apple.metal*` `export GODOT_MTL_SHADER_LOAD_STRATEGY=lazy` `<mygame> --rendering-driver metal -- --world=2 --benchmark` 17.75s user 6.19s system 17% cpu 2:15.87 total\n> \n> Got some weird artifacts though\n> \n> ![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/cec30508-18c2-471b-a28e-3da4789f55b7)\n\nI have exactly this issue. WIth lazy loading fast, but with artifcats. Need 5-10 minutes to do a proper build and then it is fast after.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3694668096/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3774669382","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/106757#issuecomment-3774669382","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106757","id":3774669382,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7g_OJG","user":{"login":"jamie-pate","id":682658,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY4MjY1OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/682658?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jamie-pate","html_url":"https://github.com/jamie-pate","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jamie-pate/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jamie-pate/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jamie-pate/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jamie-pate/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jamie-pate/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jamie-pate/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jamie-pate/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jamie-pate/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jamie-pate/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-20T19:53:35Z","updated_at":"2026-01-20T19:53:35Z","body":"16s to load in `gl_compatibility` mode.. i guess I need to add a bunch of code to tune the lighting for vulkan and opengl :(","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3774669382/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4210263990","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/106757#issuecomment-4210263990","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106757","id":4210263990,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7684e2","user":{"login":"eviltrout","id":17538,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NTM4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17538?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/eviltrout","html_url":"https://github.com/eviltrout","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eviltrout/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eviltrout/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eviltrout/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eviltrout/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eviltrout/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eviltrout/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eviltrout/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eviltrout/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eviltrout/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-08T23:03:07Z","updated_at":"2026-04-08T23:03:07Z","body":"If I clear my shaders on my current game, after the game loads (~900MB in VRAM) I'll get a spinning beach ball on mac as it compiles the metal shaders. It does this for 90s which feels like the game has crashed.\n\nThis is on a M5 MAX with 64GB of RAM, running Mac OS Tahoe 26.3.1\n\nBaking them into the .app on export seems to make no difference. (I confirmed they were in the .godot part of the exported pck)\n\nIf I add the ENV var GODOT_MTL_SHADER_LOAD_STRATEGY=lazy there is no beachball and it starts in roughly 2s.\n\nI know this means stutters can happen but on a really beefy computer having it beachball for 90s is much worse! \n\nIs this normal behaviour, or is it something pathological about my game's build? ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4210263990/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4211463261","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/106757#issuecomment-4211463261","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106757","id":4211463261,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc77BdRd","user":{"login":"Mike-Litton","id":152016512,"node_id":"U_kgDOCQ-WgA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/152016512?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mike-Litton","html_url":"https://github.com/Mike-Litton","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mike-Litton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mike-Litton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mike-Litton/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mike-Litton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mike-Litton/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mike-Litton/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mike-Litton/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mike-Litton/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mike-Litton/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-09T04:31:48Z","updated_at":"2026-04-09T04:31:48Z","body":"> If I clear my shaders on my current game, after the game loads (~900MB in VRAM) I'll get a spinning beach ball on mac as it compiles the metal shaders. It does this for 90s which feels like the game has crashed.\n> \n> This is on a M5 MAX with 64GB of RAM, running Mac OS Tahoe 26.3.1\n> \n> Baking them into the .app on export seems to make no difference. (I confirmed they were in the .godot part of the exported pck)\n> \n> If I add the ENV var GODOT_MTL_SHADER_LOAD_STRATEGY=lazy there is no beachball and it starts in roughly 2s.\n> \n> I know this means stutters can happen but on a really beefy computer having it beachball for 90s is much worse!\n> \n> Is this normal behaviour, or is it something pathological about my game's build?\n\nYou need to create some sort of ”shader compilation” system for your game. That is, if you want to avoid stutters. Also, I am guessing that your own hardware isnt all that relevant? The players are?","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4211463261/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4214471947","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/106757#issuecomment-4214471947","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106757","id":4214471947,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc77M70L","user":{"login":"eviltrout","id":17538,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NTM4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17538?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/eviltrout","html_url":"https://github.com/eviltrout","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eviltrout/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eviltrout/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eviltrout/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eviltrout/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eviltrout/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eviltrout/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eviltrout/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eviltrout/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eviltrout/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-09T13:10:59Z","updated_at":"2026-04-09T13:10:59Z","body":"> You need to create some sort of ”shader compilation” system for your game. That is, if you want to avoid stutters. \n\nI might have to add a shader compilation step. I'd tried a naive version that instantiated every material from my game but it still paused when putting the scene in the node tree because it has an environment with various settings that triggers a bunch of other shaders to be compiled.\n\n> Also, I am guessing that your own hardware isnt all that relevant? The players are?\n\nYes, but my hardware is the fastest mac you can currently buy so the players will only have a worse experience. I didn't mention this in my post but I've also reproduced this on other macs. \n\nFor now adding the ENV var above to my plist really helps things, but I am concerned because @stuartcarnie said it's not meant to be a proper option. I just don't think I could ship a game with a 90s beachball the first time it's played!\n\nIt would be a different case of course if I could query the state of Godot compiling shaders and show a progress bar. I would love if that functionality was built in with an API, but that's another issue altogether.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4214471947/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4214935969","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/106757#issuecomment-4214935969","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106757","id":4214935969,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc77OtGh","user":{"login":"Mike-Litton","id":152016512,"node_id":"U_kgDOCQ-WgA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/152016512?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mike-Litton","html_url":"https://github.com/Mike-Litton","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mike-Litton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mike-Litton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mike-Litton/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mike-Litton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mike-Litton/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mike-Litton/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mike-Litton/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mike-Litton/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mike-Litton/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-09T14:15:21Z","updated_at":"2026-04-09T14:15:21Z","body":"@eviltrout I solved in my game (released on Steam) and I tried a ton of ”programatic ways” before I settled on having small warmup scenes with crucial animations that got loaded (batched) into a larger scene with appropriate lightning and environment conditions I had to cycle true. PSO compilation is ”lethal” on any platform. There is still the occasional small variation but nothing that is noticable (even on an RTX 3050). \n\nMy own setup is an air m3 + my rtx 5080 based desktop. \n\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4214935969/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4215481844","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/106757#issuecomment-4215481844","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106757","id":4215481844,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc77QyX0","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-09T15:35:23Z","updated_at":"2026-04-09T15:35:23Z","body":"> It would be a different case of course if I could query the state of Godot compiling shaders and show a progress bar. I would love if that functionality was built in with an API, but that's another issue altogether.\n\nHow are you loading your scenes? Shader compilation should happen in the background while you load. Are you loading everything on the main thread by any chance?\n\nAlso have you read https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/tutorials/performance/pipeline_compilations.html ?","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4215481844/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4216559886","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/106757#issuecomment-4216559886","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106757","id":4216559886,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc77U5kO","user":{"login":"eviltrout","id":17538,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NTM4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17538?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/eviltrout","html_url":"https://github.com/eviltrout","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eviltrout/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eviltrout/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eviltrout/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eviltrout/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eviltrout/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eviltrout/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eviltrout/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eviltrout/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eviltrout/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-09T18:34:30Z","updated_at":"2026-04-09T18:34:30Z","body":"> How are you loading your scenes? Shader compilation should happen in the background while you load. Are you loading everything on the main thread by any chance?\n> \n> Also have you read https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/tutorials/performance/pipeline_compilations.html ?\n\nYes, I've read the pipeline doc about stutters. My problem here is not a small stutter, it's a 90s blocking thread where MTLCompilerService works on stuff before the game is playable.\n\nTo answer your question I am loading all my scenes asynchrously using the threaded loader, showing a progress bar as I do. That all loads smoothly. It's when they are added as a child to the node tree that slow blocking (beach ball on Mac) occurs.\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4216559886/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4217620430","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/106757#issuecomment-4217620430","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106757","id":4217620430,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc77Y8fO","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-09T21:24:37Z","updated_at":"2026-04-09T21:24:37Z","body":"@eviltrout What do you see in the monitors when that happens? Is there a sudden spike in \"Surface\" compilations?","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4217620430/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4950482752","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/106757#issuecomment-4950482752","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106757","id":4950482752,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABJxJfQA","user":{"login":"ernzo","id":5151357,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUxNTEzNTc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5151357?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ernzo","html_url":"https://github.com/ernzo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ernzo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ernzo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ernzo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ernzo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ernzo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ernzo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ernzo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ernzo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ernzo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-12T08:11:07Z","updated_at":"2026-07-12T11:31:10Z","body":"We've been revising the implementation with **Claude AI**, and it's possible it found and **Fixed** the root cause of:\n\n`Metal shader baking limited to SPIR-V: Unable to determine toolchain properties` on iOS export.\n\n-Two bugs on the same line in `drivers/metal/rendering_shader_container_metal.mm:82`:\n\n```cpp\n// BROKEN — escaped quotes become literal characters in the shell pattern,\n// AND the unquoted | is interpreted as a second pipe by sh -c\nparts.append_array({ \"-\", \"|\", \"grep\", \"-E\", R\"(\\\"__METAL_VERSION__|__ENVIRONMENT_OS\\\")\" });\n\n// FIXED\nparts.append_array({ \"-\", \"|\", \"grep\", \"-E\", \"'__METAL_VERSION__|__ENVIRONMENT_OS'\" });\n```\n\nAlso requires to install the MetalToolchain (not installed by default):\nxcodebuild -downloadComponent MetalToolchain`\n\n-With both fixes applied, the Export Warning disappears, \nShader Baker step completes and `.metallib` compilation runs at export time.\n\nIOW No more SPIR-V message.\n \n-The Cache files seem to be included inside the PCK file..\n\n```\n~/Projects/App Name/.godot➤ l\ntotal 240\ndrwxr-xr-x     8 cosmic  staff   256B Jul 12 12:55 .\ndrwxr-xr-x    12 cosmic  staff   384B Jul 12 12:55 ..\ndrwxr-xr-x     3 cosmic  staff    96B Jul 12 12:55 exported\n-rw-rw-r--     1 cosmic  staff   142B Jul 12 12:54 extension_list.cfg\n-rw-rw-r--     1 cosmic  staff   9.4K Jul 12 12:54 global_script_class_cache.cfg\ndrwxr-xr-x  1918 cosmic  staff    60K Jul 12 12:55 imported\ndrwxr-xr-x    30 cosmic  staff   960B Jul 12 12:55 shader_cache\n-rw-rw-r--     1 cosmic  staff   102K Jul 12 12:54 uid_cache.bin\n\n~/Projects/App Name/.godot/shader_cache➤ l\ntotal 0\ndrwxr-xr-x  30 cosmic  staff   960B Jul 12 12:55 .\ndrwxr-xr-x   8 cosmic  staff   256B Jul 12 12:55 ..\ndrwxr-xr-x   3 cosmic  staff    96B Jul 12 12:55 BlitShaderRD\ndrwxr-xr-x   3 cosmic  staff    96B Jul 12 12:55 BlurRasterShaderRD\ndrwxr-xr-x   3 cosmic  staff    96B Jul 12 12:55 BokehDofRasterShaderRD\ndrwxr-xr-x   3 cosmic  staff    96B Jul 12 12:55 CanvasOcclusionShaderRD\ndrwxr-xr-x   3 cosmic  staff    96B Jul 12 12:55 CanvasSdfShaderRD\ndrwxr-xr-x   3 cosmic  staff    96B Jul 12 12:55 CanvasShaderRD\ndrwxr-xr-x   3 cosmic  staff    96B Jul 12 12:55 CopyShaderRD\ndrwxr-xr-x   3 cosmic  staff    96B Jul 12 12:55 CopyToFbShaderRD\ndrwxr-xr-x   3 cosmic  staff    96B Jul 12 12:55 CubeToDpShaderRD\ndrwxr-xr-x   3 cosmic  staff    96B Jul 12 12:55 CubeToOctmapShaderRD\ndrwxr-xr-x   3 cosmic  staff    96B Jul 12 12:55 LuminanceReduceRasterShaderRD\ndrwxr-xr-x   3 cosmic  staff    96B Jul 12 12:55 MotionVectorsShaderRD\ndrwxr-xr-x   3 cosmic  staff    96B Jul 12 12:55 OctmapDownsamplerShaderRD\ndrwxr-xr-x   3 cosmic  staff    96B Jul 12 12:55 OctmapFilterShaderRD\ndrwxr-xr-x   3 cosmic  staff    96B Jul 12 12:55 OctmapRoughnessShaderRD\ndrwxr-xr-x   3 cosmic  staff    96B Jul 12 12:55 ParticlesCopyShaderRD\ndrwxr-xr-x   3 cosmic  staff    96B Jul 12 12:55 ParticlesShaderRD\ndrwxr-xr-x   3 cosmic  staff    96B Jul 12 12:55 ResolveRasterShaderRD\ndrwxr-xr-x   4 cosmic  staff   128B Jul 12 12:55 SceneForwardMobileShaderRD\ndrwxr-xr-x   3 cosmic  staff    96B Jul 12 12:55 ShadowFrustumShaderRD\ndrwxr-xr-x   3 cosmic  staff    96B Jul 12 12:55 SkeletonShaderRD\ndrwxr-xr-x   3 cosmic  staff    96B Jul 12 12:55 SkyShaderRD\ndrwxr-xr-x   3 cosmic  staff    96B Jul 12 12:55 SmaaBlendingShaderRD\ndrwxr-xr-x   3 cosmic  staff    96B Jul 12 12:55 SmaaEdgeDetectionShaderRD\ndrwxr-xr-x   3 cosmic  staff    96B Jul 12 12:55 SmaaWeightCalculationShaderRD\ndrwxr-xr-x   3 cosmic  staff    96B Jul 12 12:55 SortShaderRD\ndrwxr-xr-x   3 cosmic  staff    96B Jul 12 12:55 SpecularMergeShaderRD\ndrwxr-xr-x   3 cosmic  staff    96B Jul 12 12:55 TonemapMobileShaderRD\n```\n\n-On first launch the freeze on iPhone could be reduced,\nbut my app is simple 2D with just a couple shaders..\n\nCan anybody Confirm?\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4950482752/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":{"reason":"off-topic"}}]